Export point planning layer to RTZ [ECDIS Route Exchange 1.1] format to get your coordinates up in the ship's ECDIS. Set a route name, a catalog name and select an export directory. The tool will create an ECDIS compatible folder structure:

RouteExchange
----Catalog_name
--------Route_name.rtz

One route file will be created containing all (selected) points from the input layer. Route name and file name need to be identical.
Catalog name and route name will be sanitized (no weird characters).
Waypoints are ordered by "fid" or another selected field. The order of points is relevant as the ECDIS will order waypoints in the route by there order in the RTZ file, not by "id". If points are created in a different order than the one you want to have them, better create a custom order field.
The tool is fully compatible with the Cruise Tools planning universe. Navigational parameters will be added to the RTZ output, if the attributes exist in the corresponding fields. Create the planning file with Cruise Tools to avoid field name issues. The following parameters will be considered:

- Speed in knots: speed_kn
- Turn radius in nm: turn_radius_nm
- Course geometry: geometryType (can be "Orthodrome"/"Great Circle" or "Loxodrome"/"Rhumb Line")
- Cross track distance in nm: xtd_port_nm, xtd_stb_nm
- Leg report: notes

Navigational parameters of a waypoint are always valid for the leg to that waypoint.

This Tool has so far only been tested on the WÄRTSILÄ NACOS Platinum ECDIS. Use it with caution, double check your export results and create bug reports if you are having issues!
